# Risk surfaces: how much human and agent review attention a change to a path deserves.
# The pre-push review reads this file from the BASE branch, so a PR cannot lower the tier of its
# own files. Format: `<tier> <glob>`, last match wins. A glob containing `/` is anchored at the
# repository root; one without matches at any depth.
#
# critical  — correctness or durability of stored data, replication (including its wire
#             format), cluster membership, node cloning
# sensitive — authentication, authorization, keys and certificates, licensing, request
#             filtering, keeping secrets out of logs and child processes
# hot       — per-request paths where a regression is a performance incident
# ordinary  — overrides a broader line above it

critical  replication/
critical  cloneNode/
critical  bin/repairDeleteEchoRuns.ts

sensitive security/
sensitive cloneNode/jwtKeyClone.ts
sensitive cloneNode/sshKeyClone.ts
sensitive licensing/
sensitive waf/
sensitive replication/logRedaction.ts
# Closes the injected cluster-key fd before anything spawns a worker or subprocess.
sensitive bin/harper.js

ordinary  replication/blobSendWarnThrottle.ts
ordinary  replication/subscribeDeferralForTest.ts
ordinary  replication/record-lock-*-runs/
